DAY 74 - CTF CHALLENGE 4 - TRIVIAL FLAG TRANSFER PROTOCOL

Platform: picoCTF
Category: Forensics
Difficulty: Medium

WHAT IT WAS:
PCAP file with TFTP traffic containing hidden files
Flag was hidden using steganography inside picture3.bmp

TOOLS USED:
- Wireshark → filter: tftp
- File → Export Objects → TFTP (extracted all files)
- rot13.com → decoded plan file (ROT13)
- steghide → extracted hidden flag from image

STEPS:
1. Open PCAP in Wireshark
2. Filter for tftp traffic
3. Export Objects → TFTP → Save All
4. Read instruction.txt (encoded - nothing useful)
5. Read plan.txt → ROT13 encoded
6. Decoded plan → passphrase = DUEDILIGENCE
7. Ran steghide extract on all 3 bmp files
8. picture3.bmp contained flag.txt

KEY COMMANDS:
steghide extract -sf picture3.bmp
(passphrase: DUEDILIGENCE)
cat flag.txt

CONCEPTS USED:
- TFTP = Trivial File Transfer Protocol (no authentication)
- ROT13 = shift letters 13 positions (encoding not encryption)
- Steganography = hiding data inside innocent looking files
- Export Objects in Wireshark = extract files from network capture
